---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Errata" description="Corrections and errata for both editions of Teaching and Learning Mathematics Online.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Errata</p>
      <h1>Mathematics rewards corrections.</h1>
      <p>This page is the canonical place for substantive corrections to either edition. Corrections will be identified by edition, chapter, and location so that nobody has to reverse-engineer what changed.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="errata-status">
        <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Current status</p>
          <h2>No errata are posted at this time.</h2>
          <p>That is not a metaphysical claim that the books are perfect. It means there are no corrections currently published on this companion site.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How corrections will be recorded</h2>
        <p>Each item will identify the affected edition, chapter, page or section when known, the original text or issue, and the correction. Material changes will remain visible rather than silently disappearing.</p>
        <p>Publisher corrections and future-printing changes can also be noted here when they are confirmed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
